<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African Nov M3 money supply grows 15.32 pct.</title>
<headline>S.African Nov M3 money supply grows 15.32 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's year-on-year broadly defined M3 money supply grew 15.32 percent in November, preliminary Reserve Bank figures show.</p>
<p>October M3 growth was revised to 16.03 percent from a preliminary 15.96 percent.</p>
<p>Annual private sector credit growth was 17.10 percent, preliminary figures showed, against an unchanged 18.86 percent in October.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economist forecast M3 would grow at a rate of 15.5 percent in October, while they expected private sector credit extension to come in at 18.2.  </p>
<p>Detailed data (Percentage changes over 12 months):</p>
<p>Nov 1996 preliminary M3 growth -- 15.32 percent</p>
<p>Nov 1996 preliminary private sector credit growth -- 17.10 percent</p>
<p>					   Oct '96	  Sep '96</p>
<p>M3  revised			    16.03	    14.51</p>
<p>M2    &quot;				  19.52	    18.38</p>
<p>M1    &quot;				  37.16	    30.75</p>
<p>Private sector credit growth     18.86	    18.05</p>
<p>Monetary aggregates (rand millions)</p>
<p>			    Nov '96(prel) Oct '96 (rev)  Sep '96 (rev)</p>
<p>M3 unadjusted	   316.51	  311.26	   308.51</p>
<p>M3 seasonally adj.    312.94	  312.90	   309.13</p>
<p>Private sector credit 361.78	  360.97	   355.69</p>
<p>M3 annualised growth rate from base of guideline</p>
<p>			     14.54	   15.89	    15.91</p>
<p>(1996 guideline range 6-10 pct)</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
